# Prototype, and nothing here is reduced -- this is the designed form.
# `bug.json` beside this file carries what all eight hold to, and where the
# schema, the catalogue and the Check reasoning live.
#
# The designed `prototype.json` is already linear, already three steps, and
# already the one workflow carrying gateless steps by design: `frame` and
# `write_up` have no mechanical tier and no Judge in the designed form either.
#
# **This workflow carries no Judge, and that is a decision rather than an
# omission.** The designed file carries none either. A prototype is built to
# answer a question and is thrown away; there is no criterion it either meets or
# fails, so there is nothing for a veto-only Judge to refuse.
# `crates/core-model/domain/workflows.toml` names Prototype and Documentation as
# the workflows where a gateless step is the common case, not the edge one.
#
# **`build` declares no `evidence_scope`, and that is deliberate.** Decided by
# the owner Aug 28 2026, closing #146. It is the one runtime step that produces
# a diff with no declared footprint: declaring a plan for exploratory work is
# friction with no reader, and nobody is going to measure a throwaway's diff
# against a promise it had no reason to make.
#
# `build` is `human_always`, so a prototype stops for the person who asked for
# it before the write-up is drafted.
{
  "version": 1,
  "workflow_id": "prototype",
  "name": "prototype",
  "structure": "linear",
  "steps": [
    {
      "id": "frame",
      "label": "Frame",
      "evidence_type": "facts_note",
      "delivers": false,
      "advance_gate": "auto"
    },
    {
      "id": "build",
      "label": "Build",
      "evidence_type": "diff",
      "delivers": false,
      "advance_gate": "human_always"
    },
    {
      "id": "write_up",
      "label": "Write up",
      "evidence_type": "facts_note",
      "model": "haiku",
      "delivers": false,
      "advance_gate": "auto"
    }
  ]
}
